commit 5da98a31d0f0e45d9bd41c1c540224ea0ae0d194
Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 14:44:00 2026 -0800

    fix(graph): let a resumed run accept an archive move it already made

    An archive move deletes its source, so a run that failed after it (writing --emit-preview or --emit-decision) could not resume: apply read the source again and failed. The plan now carries each archived note's text; when the source is gone and the archive holds exactly that text, the move counts as done. Any other missing source still fails.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7RD9KX3HWHGKMDS0CKPM2BQ

